course: dictionary
lesson: 534
title: Atheist: a belief without God
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An atheist is a person who believes there is no God or gods. The word has two parts: "a" means not, and "theist" means someone who believes in God.
explain: «An atheist believes there is no God; an agnostic thinks we cannot know whether there is.» Here the two beliefs sit side by side, so the difference is the clue: the atheist is sure there is no God, but the agnostic says it cannot be known.
explain: Atheist can be a noun, «an atheist», or an adjective, «an atheist view». Swap in "a person who does not believe in God" and the sentence still makes sense, so you know you have the right meaning.
fact: An atheist is a person who believes there is no God or gods.
fact: As an adjective, atheist describes such a person or view, as in «an atheist view».
fact: Theists believe in God, atheists do not, and agnostics say they cannot know.
fact: Atheists can be kind and moral, just as religious people can.
fact: Respect for different beliefs is part of school values.
exercise: «An atheist believes there is no God; an agnostic thinks we cannot know whether there is.» What does an atheist believe? | Everyone must pray every day | *There is no God or gods | We cannot know anything about God | There is a God who watches over everyone
exercise: Which is true about atheists? | *Atheists can be kind and moral, just as religious people can | Atheists are always angry | All atheists live in the same town | Atheists cannot be kind or fair
exercise: In «An atheist is someone who does not believe in God; secular means not religious.» which word means not religious? | atheist | *secular | someone | believe
test: The phrase «an atheist view» means | A view that God is everywhere | A view that all children must go to church | A view that we cannot know if God exists | *A view that there is no God
test: Sam says atheist and agnostic mean the same. What is the difference? | Agnostics believe in God | They are two names for the same thing | *An atheist believes there is no God; an agnostic thinks we cannot know | Atheists are always angry
exam: In «Religious answers include Christianity, Islam, Judaism, Hinduism, Sikhism, Buddhism and many more; non-religious people, like atheists, give answers without God.» what do atheists give? | Answers that everyone must follow | Answers that are always the same | Answers with a prayer at the start | *Answers without God
